What is Elastic Load Balancing (ELB)?

An Elastic Load Balancer (ELB) automatically distributes incoming traffic across multiple targets.

Targets can be:

EC2 Instances
Containers (ECS/EKS)
Lambda Functions (ALB)
IP addresses

ELB automatically:

Detects unhealthy servers
Routes traffic only to healthy servers
Supports SSL termination
Scales automatically
Types of AWS Load Balancers

AWS provides four types.

Load Balancer	OSI Layer	Best For
Application Load Balancer (ALB)	Layer 7	HTTP/HTTPS
Network Load Balancer (NLB)	Layer 4	TCP/UDP
Gateway Load Balancer (GWLB)	Layer 3/4	Network appliances
Classic Load Balancer (CLB)	Layer 4 & 7	Legacy workloads
